.syl/
node_modules/
coverage/
dist/

# The build a deploy can roll back to. Same shape as dist/, kept beside it
# rather than inside it so a build cannot copy the previous one into the new
# one recursively. Machine state, never source.
.dist-previous/

# Agent worktrees live inside the repo. Never track them: committing a
# worktree's contents is how adj-204 broke the entire Adjutant fleet — a
# node_modules symlink pointing into a peer worktree got committed to main,
# and every fresh checkout recreated it broken.
worktrees/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
# A leading path segment anchors a pattern to the repo root, so this only ever
# matched a run started from here — and `npm run verify` writes the file into
# whichever WORKSPACE it ran in. `backend/tests/.vitest-results.json` therefore
# showed up as untracked for anyone who ran the gate the documented way.
#
# The glob covers the per-pass files too. The suite runs as two vitest
# processes — `.vitest-results.light.json` and `.vitest-results.heavy.json`,
# one each — so a pattern naming only the old single file would start leaving
# untracked results behind the day the split landed.
**/tests/.vitest-results*.json

# Apple signing and push keys. NEVER commit these.
#
# The Commander copied AuthKey_XXTN5423K8.p8 into this directory so the launchd
# install can reference it locally. It is an APNs auth key: whoever holds it can
# send push notifications to every app in the team, and Apple's limit is TWO KEYS
# PER TEAM, so a leak is expensive to remediate as well as dangerous.
#
# Broad by extension rather than by filename, because the next key will have a
# different name and a .gitignore that only knows about today's is a guard that
# stops working the moment it matters.
*.p8
*.p12
*.cer
*.mobileprovision
*.keystore

# Source media for the app. Large, and the encoded copies that ship live in
# ios/Syl/Resources — keeping both in git would double the weight for no gain.
assets/*.mp4
